  "notes": "The source-visible title page describes a Russian translation from German but names no translator. A contemporary 1901 report associates the uncredited Reader book with material reprinted from the New Journal and therefore with Antonovsky's historical route, but no collation or source-page credit closes that responsibility. The Expression remains distinct and provisional; no identity, derivation, or equivalence with the 1898, 1900, or later Antonovsky states is materialized.",
